WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:04.960
Speaker 1: Hey, this is a pretty big&nbsp;
deal. Former Attorney General Eric Holder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:12.000
is now predicting that Donald Trump and his&nbsp;
top administration officials will be indicted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.800
will be indicted. Newsweek writes Former Attorney&nbsp;
General Eric Holder predicted Friday that Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.800
as well as other top officials from the former&nbsp;
president's administration, will be invited by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.520
indicted by the U.S. government over the events of&nbsp;
January six, 2021, and their efforts to change the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:38.240
2020 results. In early May, Holder told CBS News&nbsp;
he believed Trump's actions related to January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.960
six merit an indictment. Hundreds of Trump&nbsp;
supporters attacked the U.S. Capitol that day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.000
after the then president told them to walk to the&nbsp;
federal legislative building and fight like hell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.120
to save their country. Those directions came&nbsp;
after Trump claimed for months that Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:59.280
victory was fraudulent while pressuring officials&nbsp;
across the country to overturn the win. On Friday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.840
in an interview on HBO's Real Time with&nbsp;
Bill Maher, Holder reiterated his view&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:12.640
that Trump should face indictment. Let's take&nbsp;
a look at this video of Eric Holder explaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.760
this here to Bill Maher on his show Friday.
Speaker 2: If you were still the attorney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.640
general about Trump and January six, well, I'll&nbsp;
tell you, if you'd asked me that question about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.520
year or so ago, I would have said I. Been awfully&nbsp;
concerned about the divisive nature of bringing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.320
case against a former president. But now, because&nbsp;
of what we know, what great journalists have done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.880
the leaks that have come from the January six&nbsp;
committee, if you show me that Donald Trump was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:43.280
involved in the efforts to, in essence, foment&nbsp;
a coup, and you can show the requisite intent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.040
he has to be indicted.
Unidentified:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.400
And what would that entail after you indict him?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.560
After you indict him? Well, he would.
